what up space fam golson here from anime  upper and i'm back at it again to  discuss the latest and craziest  developments in the one piece story  today we got zorro vs king conclusion  luffy vs kaido and much more so make  sure to stay tuned for this one if you  do enjoy seeing these one-piece reviews  and want to keep them coming channel the  pirate king within and smash that like  button with no mercy remember smashing  that like button is pirate king energy  and passing is orochi energy so choose  wisely if you haven't make this the  video subscribe and hit that  notification bell to turn on all  notifications or you will miss future  one-piece videos and updates and while  you wait for the next one-piece chapter  to drop feel free to check out my huge  and growing one-piece playlist that  includes videos called the yonko admiral  supernova and much more link to that is  in the description now without further  ado let's jump into it spoilers and all  this chapter is called bushido is the  way of death which is a quote taken from  a guide to being a warrior samurai and  although we tend to respect people who  are ready to face down death in the  pursuit of their principles and dreams  it's interesting how they play with the  concept in this chapter but more on that  later our boy zorro has done the  impossible arzoro the dude we watched  since back when he was luffy's only  crewmate just beat king the strongest  creature's right hand man the yonko  commander with the highest known bounty  it just feels surreal this is actually  happening and it's crazy the narrator  says zorro clipped king's wings which is  pretty epic from our perspective since  we back zorro but pretty sad for king at  the same time and they've done a good  job of making us sympathize with him  through the flashbacks king remembers a  conversation with kaido where he said he  believed kaido was joy boy king said it  doesn't matter what kaido does he owes  his life to him he tells kaido to keep  being the strongest and he'll make sure  to never lose until kaido is the king of  the pirates and it's genuinely a bit sad  that he couldn't keep his promise you  can tell that king's a solid dude and  lives by his principles so it isn't just  a purely satisfying defeat like when  sanji beat up queen who has such a  hateable personality and let's keep in  mind king did a good job he was clearly  significantly younger in the flashbacks  and now he's 47 years old in his defense  he gave kaido plenty of time to become  the pirate king so he shouldn't feel too  bad about his loss it's just crazy that  he lost to an up-and-coming 21 year old  imagine zorro at 47 it's actually insane  how well the straw hats are doing based  on their ages we then get king's  backstory juxtaposed to zorro's  backstory when zorro lost and promised  to never lose again and ask the king of  the pirates aka luffy if he had a  problem with that luffy laughed and said  nope oda is doing a good job here of  showing that even though arzoro got to  keep his promise it also meant another  person another solid dude failing to  keep his it's the harsh reality that on  the path to be the best there will be  many people whose dreams get crushed and  zorro is so cool here he says if this is  what it takes he'll become the king of  hell to fulfill his promise and reach  his dream it's interesting that our main  character is associated with hell here  while the antagonist king looks like a  fallen or defeated angel he cut down but  it goes well with one piece and how  luffy also insists that he's not the  good guy he's a pirate who does what he  wants to do anyways zorro despite just  beating the yonko commander still has  enough energy to launch a powerful  attack that propels him back onto the  island shocking and very hyped stuff  we've seen from zorro this arc and this  dude definitely earned to get some rest  at this point i felt like it was over  last chapter 2 but this was a fitting  way to end this fight and nice to get it  spelled out for us by the narrator that  the victor is in fact zorro no more  doubt about it a cp-0 member hears that  king has lost and he straight up says it  can't be and yeah that must be how it  will feel to the whole world when this  gets out the all-stars and the flying  six are defeated as is mentioned it's no  joke but it's also mentioned that with  those two monsters meaning big mom and  kaido still going those wins are  meaningless and that's a bit harsh  saying they're meaningless since we know  the last battle had hella meaning for  both zorro and king but yeah i get where  he's coming from in the sense that two  yonko could take out an army on their  own and until both of them fall or at  least one of them falls this is far from  over we see big mom against kit and law  still going strong and honestly this is  the fight that i'm most concerned about  in the sense that i don't know how our  side will win i trust luffy i know he'll  pull it off but things are just not  looking good for law and kid we'll see  this is definitely one of the fights  that i'm glued to the most and i'm just  very curious to see what will happen the  whole island about to hit the city thing  is explained again if nothing happens it  will crash into it if kaido loses it'll  fall and explode because of the  stockpiled weapons and if momo creates  the clouds to hold it up kanjura's  revenge flames could set off the  explosives anyways so yamato will have  to stop it in all likelihood momo will  succeed and yamato will succeed and  that's how our team will survive we get  fuga helping yamato by attacking another  number guarding a door it's great  because instead of getting the key as  asked fuga just smashes through the  other number and the door at the same  time it's such a great scene for this  high pace point in the arc then we have  our boy usop shine and this is where the  constant readiness of death comes in  both kinemon and kiku think they're too  far gone and usopp should rescue the  other and usopp hilariously says perfect  i'll just leave you both an escape which  made me laugh but then he does the right  thing like always and he's like this is  enough of this dying stuff the whole  point of the rescue attempt is to save  them and they shouldn't be so resigned  to death and it's an interesting idea  taking fearlessness and honor too far  usab gives a nice and pretty convincing  alternate life view saying and i quote  it may look pathetic to keep struggling  with tears and snot running down my face  but i don't care i'll never stop  clinging to life you have to keep going  even if it's in disgrace dying after  coming this far would be a waste end  quote great speech great logic and it  appears his words and perhaps tears  really reach the two who were stoically  resigned to die just a few moments ago i  gotta admit watching zorro and samurai  and even batman ready to die if that's  what it takes is inspiring af but it can  be taken to an extreme and dying is not  always necessary so i really like that  oda communicates this through usopp here  nobody should give up on life so easily  if it's possible to survive izo agrees  and comes to protect usopp and the  others it's a very cool moment iso is  recognized by enemies as a former  whitebeard division leader but usopp  doesn't know who he is iso in a very  well done panel reveals his back and the  kozuki family symbol on it he's right to  protect the others and tells them if  they truly believe in luffy they have to  live on after all if they live on they  can be of more use to the cause down the  line izo even calls god usa by name and  tells him to keep them safe usab said he  didn't know who iso was but izo knew of  him showing how famous the straw hats  have become and it's not lost on usa  that such a clearly legendary fighter  knows him either it's a great moment  where he tries to live up to his own  hype and take care of them and then we  just get some more updates on characters  like the ninja is still fighting and  it's pretty even and orochi's still  wondering if he's dreaming and  distracted by his komurasaki as the  whole place is about to blow apu instead  of fighting honorably like drake did  against cp 0 runs away i wonder if it  would have made any difference if he had  drake's back and they fought together  but as things are they have taken out  drake a supernova proving to be very  formidable fighters notably though they  do give him some praise for being a  handful thus we didn't really get the  all-out apu and drake versus these two  because apu just ran away and i guess we  could all see that coming i feel bad for  drake though but this fall served to  show us that these guys are in fact  quite strong and robin better watch out  suddenly they are told to get out of the  castle quickly since the all-stars have  been wiped out so that might actually be  the thing that gets them off robin's  back unless they just use his motivation  to increase the speed of their search  either way looks good for supernova apu  since they have no time to waste with  him it's said the chance of the new  generation winning is a million to one  but they gotta be ready if they somehow  pull it off and it's definitely looking  more likely by the chapter we also see  that zorro and sanjay are recovering and  not in fighting shape which makes sense  they did enough we get a hype statement  that news that big like the straw hat's  beating to yonko would exacerbate  everything that's happening in the world  the fate of an era will be decided on  this island in the next few minutes wow  things just don't get more hyped than  that oh it is pretty much telling us the  next few chapters will be insane  pandemonium the cp0 agents want to  believe that the straw hats and friends  have reached their limit but as if in  defiance of that statement we see luffy  still going strong taking hits from  kaido and even dishing out a great punch  that sends kaido flying luffy falls too  and then they both get up it's such a  great moment as they are both loving it  they're both bosses and this is what you  get when bosses fight they're excited by  the challenge and both think it's  getting good the narrator tells us that  these are the smiles of the mighty and  then asks what will the fallout of this  death match be another hype detail  suggests that kaido might straight up be  killed but maybe death match is just  used for dramatic effect here either way  i am shocked by how well the straw hats  have done but also worried that as cp 0  mentioned they they're reaching their  limit even if luffy wins he'll be tired  sanji and zorro are down right now so a  full-on marine attack after this will  not be good they'll definitely need some  help to get out of this insane situation  but that is it for this one for this  chapter one piece is so good right now  and getting better this is a historic  moment for the manga no doubt mvp here  goes to usopp for me because of his epic  speech i really loved it and luffy was  great too don't get me wrong but he'll  probably get mvp for like the next  couple of chapters in a row anyways let  me know who your mvp was and what you  expect to happen in the next chapter  what do you think will happen to big mom  if the marines fail to time their attack  well enough big mom might actually join  forces with our guys to escape as usual  we'll see what happens it's gonna be  crazy no matter what happens we know  that for sure but anyways if you did  enjoy this review and want to keep them  coming chill the pirate king within and  smash that like button with no mercy go  luffy on it go joy boy on it go roger on  it remember smashing that like button is  pirate king energy and passing is energy  so choose wisely if you haven't make  this the video subscribe and this is  crucial hit that notification bell to  turn on all notifications or you will  miss future one-piece videos and updates  and while you wait for the next  one-piece chapter to drop feel free to  check out my huge one-piece playlist  that includes videos of the yonko  admiral supernova and much more link to  that is in the description and until  next time see ya space cowboys  [Music]  you

